#!/bin/sh
# bwrap as AirDrop asks it, to read the picture a sender sends with its
# offer in a sandbox: the call noted in $HOME/stub-calls, as `record` notes
# one, and the command after its options run as it is, outside any sandbox.
# The files it binds are bound where they are, so the command's paths are
# the same outside.
printf 'bwrap' >>"$HOME/stub-calls"
for word in "$@"; do printf ' %s' "$word" >>"$HOME/stub-calls"; done
printf '\n' >>"$HOME/stub-calls"
while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do
  case $1 in
    --setenv | --ro-bind | --bind | --symlink) shift 3 ;;
    --cap-drop | --proc | --dev | --tmpfs) shift 2 ;;
    --*) shift ;;
    *) break ;;
  esac
done
exec "$@"
